== Std.Terminal (r3.88): ReadKey reads the keys of a terminal from the bytes
== of standard input, so a pipe or a file tests it: characters in UTF-8,
== Ctrl+letter, the escape sequences of the arrows, Home/End/PageUp/PageDown,
== Delete and F1..F12 (with xterm modifiers), Escape then a key as Alt, and a
== lone Escape at the end. RawMode does nothing when input is not a terminal,
== and ScreenSize is 24 x 80 when output is not one.
Use Std.Terminal

Main :
    RawMode(True)
    Size := ScreenSize
    PutLn(Size.Rows, " ", Size.Cols)
    for Index in 1..15
        Key := ReadKey
        PutLn(Index, " ", Key.Kind, " ", Integer(Key.Ch), " ", Key.Ctrl, " ", Key.Alt)
    ;
    RawMode(False)
    Last := ReadKey
    PutLn(Last.Kind)
;
